{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"toadish-unrivaled-carp","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nRunning `uv` in this checkout generates a `uv.lock` at the repo root that shows up as an untracked file. rebar deliberately keeps core dependencies unpinned (`>=`), and `.github/dependabot.yml` states a `uv` ecosystem block should be added only \"if a uv.lock is ever committed\" — so the lockfile is a per-developer artifact that must not be tracked.\n\n## Approach\nAdd a `uv.lock` entry to `.gitignore` with an explanatory comment matching the file's existing commented style, placed alongside the other per-developer tooling ignore rules (e.g. `.serena/`, `.tokensave/`). No dependency-manifest change — core deps stay unpinned `>=` by design; this only stops an already-uncommitted artifact from appearing as untracked.\n\n## Scope\n- `.gitignore` — add a commented `uv.lock` ignore rule.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `.gitignore` contains a `uv.lock` rule; verified by `git check-ignore uv.lock` printing `uv.lock` and exiting 0.\n- [ ] A stray root `uv.lock` no longer appears in `git status --porcelain`.\n- [ ] No other tracked files change; verified by `git diff --stat` on the change showing only `.gitignore`.","id":"856c-4282-53e0-4d77","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Ignore per-developer uv.lock in .gitignore"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785619916847962001,"uuid":"1ebddfc6-d35a-49f3-a70b-b3d99bad448f"}